# Lyceum: the depth plan (Track C, after Track A, before Amsterdam)

> **What this file is.** The second plan over the built tree. Track A gave Lyceum its loop, its theme, its characters, its deck and its film. This plan gives it depth: a course record a quality office would recognise, a semester of teaching material, the two student surveys, attainment computed the way Malaysian universities report it, a before and after a judge can see, and a judge's own way through the app with the host as the guide. It plans only. Nothing in it is built, captured or rendered until the owner says so, and recording is gated to the end (Section 0.3).

**Stamp.**

- Written: 22 October 2026, evening, Kuala Lumpur time, by the planning session that wrote the four research notes it cites.
- Over: `main` after the A8 commit (`b4bfdc4`) plus the owner's uncommitted follow-ups of 22 October, as [as-built.md](as-built.md) records them (stamp 15:05). Where this plan and the code disagree about what exists, the code and the as-built record win; where this plan and [lyceum-upgrade-plan.md](lyceum-upgrade-plan.md) disagree about what to build next, this plan wins, because it is later and was written against the built tree.
- For: the HACKaSTONE 2026 Grand Final, Thursday 29 October 2026, Amsterdam ([competition/grand-final-2026.md](competition/grand-final-2026.md)).
