## 10. Assessment items and exports

Smallest useful version, last in the order:

- `src/lib/items.ts`: deterministic item templates per Bloom level using the Arkansas verb list (remember: list, define, name; understand: explain, paraphrase, summarise; apply: calculate, demonstrate, use; analyse: classify, diagram, break down; evaluate: judge, defend, justify; create: design, formulate, compose), the course topic's `misconceptions` as distractors, and the outcome's words in the stem. Multiple choice with three or four options, short answer and essay.
- The Haladyna lint, each rule named on screen: a positive stem that carries the main idea; three or four options; one keyed answer with its position varied; options of similar length; no "all of the above" or "none of the above"; no absolutes; no grammar clue; distractors from recorded misconceptions. An item that fails a rule shows the rule and cannot be exported.
- Exports from one item model: Moodle XML first (UTP's ULearn is Moodle; `multichoice`, `shortanswer`, `essay` with the elements the research lists), QTI 2.1 second (Canvas and Blackboard Ultra), QTI 3.0 later; the rubric grid to XLSX through SheetJS.
- Where: the Teach step's session card, "Check for understanding" becomes items with the lint beside them and "Export for Moodle (.xml)"; the week 7 quiz in the sample has ten items that pass the lint.
- The old test-draft flow in the sandbox is left as it is and labelled illustrative, as today.

## 11. The data model and the migration

- Backup schema 6. `LATER_DEFAULTS` in `src/lib/workspaceBackup.ts` gains `institution`, `programme.plos`, `surveys`, `surveyResponses`, `cqiNotes`, `rubrics`; the course definition, topic, outcome, session and result-row additions are optional fields with defaults applied on restore. `scripts/check-backup-migration.mjs` restores schemas 3, 4, 5 and 6.
- New event kinds: `grades-released`, `survey-opened`, `survey-collected`, `cqi-noted`. The How it works timeline reads them as it reads the others.
- `ResultUpload.rows[].atOrAbove`, `bins`; `SurveyResponse` (formId, term, answers keyed by question id, collectedAt, source: booth, pasted, imported, sample); never a student identifier.
- The moods: Lens is "waiting" while survey responses await collection and "done" when an OBE report or a CQI note is saved; Prism "done" when slides are saved; Folio "done" when the course file is exported. `prove-moods` keeps every mood a pure function of records.
- The loop's done rules are unchanged (Section 4 of the master plan); the richer record changes no rule.

## 12. Checks, documentation and the sample workspace

- New suites, registered in `prove:all` and in `src/data/suites.ts`: `prove-course-record` (the sample validates; SLT sums to 120; weights sum to 100; every CLO is assessed; every topic links an outcome; the matrix has a level in every cell that is linked; the course file zip lists its parts and the manifest marks what is not included), `prove-materials` (fourteen packs render and unzip; every slide has a unique title and notes; body text is 18 pt or larger; the mark appears once per content slide; the preview SVG lists the same slides as the file), `prove-surveys` (the definitions; the URL round trip; the importers on the three fixtures; the floor; the lock), `prove-attainment` (the KPI arithmetic on the fixture; the PLO roll-up; the migration of a row without `atOrAbove`), `prove-diff` (word diff, deltas, the slide diff, the counters), `prove-judge` (every walk stop's `data-demo-id` exists on its screen; the kiosk returns; the recap's numbers equal the records they cite). The four smokes gain the judge's page, the walk by keyboard, the course file download, the survey's booth round trip and the compare view at 320 px.
- `node mcp/sample.ts` regenerates the sample workspace from the tour's end state and the door's proof asserts the new tools. `node scripts/generate-guide.mjs --check` after the section guides gain Judge, Recap and Institution. The contrast check with the partner-mark exclusion. The dash scan. The backup migration check.
- `docs/as-built.md` gains the Track C changelog and the dated verification table; `docs/claims.md` gains any figure a judge-facing surface shows that is not synthetic (the check count row changes by the check); `docs/doors.md` gains the two tools; `docs/lecturer-guide.md` regenerates; `README.md` gains the judge's page and the course file under the existing headings, with its screenshots untouched until D9.
- `CLAUDE.md`'s read order gains one line after item 1: this plan, and the four research notes it cites by name (D0).

