```

## 16. Running it as one autonomous session

The protocol of master plan 17.5 applies with these changes: the order is Section 14.1's; the permissions granted in advance are the same (commit after every package with a plain message and no attribution trailer, install the npm packages this plan names, create and delete files inside the repository, run every check, smoke and generator that is not gated); the gated commands of Section 0.2 are added to the never list, along with "never edit a tour caption or reorder the tour, never send files to Codex except the two reviews in Section 15 and only on the owner's go in this session, never put the UTP mark on the landing page, the poster or the deck before Section 18 item 2 is answered". Decisions go to `docs/decisions.md` in the fixed shape; questions go to Needs the owner in `docs/run-log.md`; the run continues with the next package that does not depend on the answer.

**The driver prompt** (copy as one message):

```text
You are running Track C of docs/lyceum-depth-plan.md on your own. Read CLAUDE.md, then the depth plan in full, then docs/as-built.md Sections 1, 2, 5 and 6, docs/decisions.md from "12:00, after Track A" to the end, docs/competition/grand-final-2026.md, and the four research notes the plan cites in Section 20, before anything else; re-read the plan's Section 16 and docs/run-log.md at the start of every package. Do not work from memory: when the plan and the code disagree about what exists, read the code and log the difference.

Work through the packages in this order, one at a time, finishing and committing each before the next: D0, D1, D2, D5, D6, D8 (Tier 1); then D3, D4 and D8 again (Tier 2); then D7 and D8 again (Tier 3). The session prompt in Section 17 is each package's specification. Do not stop between packages. You have my permission in advance, so do not ask: commit after every package with a plain message and no attribution trailer; install the npm packages the plan names (lz-string; nothing else without a decision logged); create and delete files inside this repository; run every check, smoke and generator that the plan does not gate.

Never: run npm run shots, node video/capture/capture.mjs, any Remotion render or the determinism check, npm run gen:sample-decks, npm run deck, node scripts/gen-brief-pdf.mjs or node scripts/gen-poster.mjs, or copy screenshots into the README (those are D9 and wait for my written go); edit a caption in src/demo/script.ts or reorder the tour; push to any remote; tag amsterdam-2026; spend money; send anything off this machine, including to Codex, unless I say so in this session; use a third-party skill without the SkillSpector scan; put the UTP mark on the landing page, the poster or the deck; change the main idea, the six steps, the palette, the honesty labels or the dates. Every sample record, slide, response and mark you write is synthetic and is labelled so, and every surface that shows the UTP mark carries the demo line from the plan's Section 3.3.

