## 18. Needs the owner, before the run

1. **Sample content authorship.** Rule 0.2.4 reads the runtime rule as applying to runtime: the course record, the slides, the lab sheets, the quiz and the survey responses are written by the build session as reviewed fixtures, labelled sample. Confirm, or name a teammate who will author or review them instead (the Story lane, or the lecturer on the team).
2. **The UTP mark.** In the app's sample material and the pack, labelled demo: confirm. On the public landing page, the poster, the deck and the film: only after you confirm with the university, or never. Until answered, the mark stays off those surfaces.
3. **The booth collector.** Recommended: the local API on the booth laptop over the team's own hotspot, no third party, with the paste code as the fallback. Alternative: a Cloudflare Worker on your account (free tier, sends responses off the machine). Choose.
4. **Hardware.** A second screen on a stand (the research's packing list), and the thermal printer for printed receipts (optional, only if one is to hand). Choose.
5. **The record day.** D9 runs only on your word; the best moment is after Tier 2 lands and you have seen the screens, which the schedule puts on Sunday 25 or Monday 26. Say when.
6. **The deck.** Slides 6 and 7 change at D9 to carry the before and after and the OBE table; the receipt on slide 1 and the five figures do not change. Confirm, or keep the deck as it is and show the new screens only in the booth.
7. **Open from Track A.** TRL 6 or TRL 5 (run-log item 4), the pitch's opening order (item 5), the GitHub description (item 6), the Claude Desktop run (item 2), the flight time that sets the freeze.

## 19. Risks

| Risk | Why it matters | Guard |
|:--|:--|:--|
| The sample course breaks the tour | The tour targets `data-demo-id`s and types into fields that D1 redesigns | D1 keeps every id or remaps it in the same session; `npm run smoke` is in D1's verification; captions untouched |
| Four days is not enough | D2's content and D5's eight views are the long ones | Tiers; D6 and D8 before Tier 2; cut D7 first, then D3's campus exports, then the programme wall |
| The 500 kB bundle advisory grows | The compare views and the preview add code | `jszip` and the DOCX writer behind dynamic import like pptxgenjs; measured in D8 |
| The contrast check and the partner mark | A third-party SVG carries non-token colours | The exclusion in D0 with its reason; the mark never inlined |
| pptxgenjs issue 1449 | String shape presets write invalid XML | Shape constants; the proof reads the XML; the repair only if the proof finds the fault |
| PDPA and consent | A survey of students collects personal data in a real deployment | No identifiers stored; the consent line; the floor; the lock; the policy note is Track B's `docs/learning-analytics-policy.md` |
| Realism of the course record | A quality officer on the panel will know a thin course file | The EAC and MQA lists in Section 4.1; the external examiner review by Codex after D2; the manifest that names its own gaps |
| The KPI reads as UTP's rule | It is UTHM's practice from the research, not a UTP document | The profile's help text and the research note say so; the threshold is a setting |
| Someone records anyway | The owner's credit and time | The gate in the driver prompt's never list; D9 is the only package that names those commands |

